msgid "# GLM-5.3-Flash (Experimental)"
msgstr "# GLM-5.3-Flash（实验性）"

msgid "## 1 Introduction"
msgstr "## 1 简介"

msgid ""
"[GLM-5.3-Flash](https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash) is the first "
"natively multimodal model in the GLM-5 series. Built on a hybrid "
"architecture that combines sparse and linear attention for the first time in"
" the GLM series, it adopts Manifold-Constrained Hyper-Connections (mHC) and "
"is trained on a 30T-token multimodal pre-training corpus. With 320B total "
"parameters and only 18B active parameters, it outperforms GLM-5.2 across "
"benchmarks and real-world workloads at one-tenth the price, while "
"approaching Claude Opus 4.8 on coding and agentic benchmarks. GLM-5.3-Flash "
"also supports controlling the thinking budget through the `reasoning_effort`"
" parameter (`low`, `high`, `max`)."
msgstr ""
"[GLM-5.3-Flash](https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash) 是 GLM-5 "
"系列中首个原生多模态模型。它基于 GLM 系列中首次结合稀疏注意力和线性注意力的混合架构构建，采用流形约束超连接（mHC），并在 30T token "
"的多模态预训练语料上进行训练。该模型总参数量为 320B，但仅有 18B 激活参数，在基准测试和实际工作负载上以十分之一的价格超越 "
"GLM-5.2，同时在编码和智能体基准上接近 Claude Opus 4.8。GLM-5.3-Flash 还支持通过 "
"`reasoning_effort` 参数（`low`、`high`、`max`）控制思考预算。"

